LOCATION:Miller 102
SUMMARY:Visiting Artist Rosemary Holliday Hall
DESCRIPTION:The Department of Art &amp\; Art History is excited to host R
 osemary Holliday Hall–artist and ecologist–as a visiting artist in ce
 ramics and biology the week of April 6. She will present a public lecture
  about her artistic practice at 4:30pm on Wednesday April 8 in Miller 102
 .Rosemary Holliday Hall (https://rosemaryhollidayhall.com/)'s transdiscip
 linary practice spans installation\, sculpture\, ceramics\, sound\, movin
 g image\, and performance. Her work explores the intersections of insects
 \, plants\, and people\, and the possibility of cross pollination between
  forms of knowledge including scientific\, embodied\, ancestral\, and art
 istic. She engages with research through close observation\, and is espec
 ially interested in relational ecologies between species.Hall holds an MF
 A from the School of the Art Institute of Chicago and a BFA with a minor 
 in Environmental Horticulture from the University of California\, Davis. 
 Her work has been exhibited in both solo and group exhibitions across the
  United States and internationally.  The lecture is sponsored by the Swan
 son Fund and the Department of Art &amp\; Art History
