SUMMARY:Live Podcast Recording and Q&A with Mark Goldberg\, host of Globa
 l Perspectives and To Save Us From Hell
DESCRIPTION:Mark Leon Goldberg is a veteran international affairs journal
 ist who writes the Global Dispatches (https://www.globaldispatches.org/) 
 Substack and hosts the Global Dispatches podcast (https://www.globaldispa
 tches.org/p/get-the-global-dispatches-podcast?r=bk3k&amp\;utm_campaign=po
 st&amp\;utm_medium=web&amp\;triedRedirect=true&amp\;_src_ref=globaldispat
 ches.org) — the longest running international affairs podcast\, named b
 y The Guardian as a "podcast to make you smarter." He also hosts To Save 
 Us From Hell (https://www.globaldispatches.org/s/to-save-us-from-hell)\, 
 a podcast that discusses the players and debates raging at the UN to keep
  us from that fiery furnace.  Mark has been recognized as a pioneer of "h
 umanitarian journalism" that combines the conventions of journalism (like
  objectivity) with key principles of global humanitarianism (like the mor
 al equivalence of all lives). This often leads him to shine a spotlight o
 n under-covered global stories. Mark's work has been features in the New 
 York Times\, The Guardian\, The American Prospect\, Foreign Policy\, The 
 Globe and Mail\, The Los Angeles Times\, Newsweek\, The New Republic\, an
 d The Daily Beast. He has appeared regularly as an on-air guest for Al Ja
 zeera English\, National Public Radio\, the BBC\, and CSPAN.  Come attend
  this live podcast recording where Mark has a conversation with Kyle Lasc
 urettes\, Chair of the International Affairs department\, on the role and
  future of international organizations in addressing democratic erosion a
 nd authoritarian resurgence. We would love to see student participation i
 n the Q&amp\;A as part of the podcast! Snacks will be provided.
