 g/s/to-save-us-from-hell&amp\;source=gmail&amp\;ust=1773438049339000&amp\
 ;usg=AOvVaw08iEcSMQ50VKRw9_M2ew2M">To Save Us From Hell</a>\, a podcast t
 hat discusses the players and debates raging at the UN to keep us from th
 at fiery furnace.</p><p>  Mark has been recognized as a pioneer of "human
 itarian journalism" that combines the conventions of journalism (like obj
 ectivity) with key principles of global humanitarianism (like the moral e
 quivalence of all lives). This often leads him to shine a spotlight on un
 der-covered global stories. Mark's work has been features in the <em>New 
 York Times\, The Guardian\, The American Prospect\, Foreign Policy\, The 
 Globe and Mail\, The Los Angeles Times\, Newsweek\, The New Republic\,</e
 m> and <em>The Daily Beast.</em> He has appeared regularly as an on-air g
 uest for <em>Al Jazeera English\, National Public Radio\,</em> the <em>BB
 C\,</em> and <em>CSPAN.</em></p><p>  Come attend this live podcast record
 ing where Mark has a conversation with Kyle Lascurettes\, Chair of the In
 ternational Affairs department\, on the role and future of international 
