DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260411T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260411T170000
SUMMARY:Auditions for Fall 2026 MainStage Musical
DESCRIPTION:Come audition for the Fall MainStage Musical:  Natasha\, Pier
 re &amp\; the Great Comet of 1812Music Auditions: 10-2:30pm in Seitz Loun
 ge in Evans Music CenterDance Auditions: 3-5pm in Fir Acres BlackboxThe T
 heatre &amp\; Dance and Music Departments will hold pre-auditions this sp
 ring for a few roles in the Fall 2026 MainStage Musical.&#160\; (Audition
 s will be held again in Fall 2026 for roles that are not filled.) Sign up
  on the Call Board in Fir Acres Theatre.Dance Auditions:  For the dance a
 udition performers should be prepared to learn and perform a short combin
 ation demonstrating basic movement ability\, musicality\, coordination\, 
 and performance presence. Dancers may briefly share any prior training\, 
 technical skills\, or movement strengths they have\, including turns\, le
 aps\, acro\, or other dance styles. Audition focus is not only on technic
 al ability\, but also on adaptability\, confidence\, and responsiveness t
 o instruction.The music audition will consist of three elements:A range c
 heck (warmup)  An unaccompanied folk song or pop song of your choosing  A
  song from the list below that corresponds to the character you are inter
 ested in    The following song suggestions for each character draw from a
  wide range of musicals and pop/rock music\, chosen to align with the cha
 racters' complexities\, emotions\, and the vocal demands of the roles. Th
 e list below is certainly not meant to be the only songs we want to hear\
 , but ideas about the type of song.You are expected to bring sheet music 
 for your song from this list. If you need help finding the sheet music pl
 ease contact Prof. Cox (lc21-1459@lclark.edu (mailto:lc21-1459@lclark.edu
 )) or Sue McBerry (mcberry@lclark.edu (mailto:mcberry@lclark.edu)) or ema
 il theatre@lclark.edu (mailto:theatre@lclark.edu)&#160\;  Pierre Bezukhov
 "Anthem" from Chess    Natasha Rostova"I Feel Pretty" from West Side Stor
 y    Andrey Bolkonsky"Johanna (Reprise)" from Sweeney Todd    Anatole Kur
 agin"Left Behind" from Spring Awakening    Hélène Bezukhova"The Ladies 
 Who Lunch" from Company    Marya D"Send in the Clowns" from A Little Nigh
 t Music    Sonya"On My Own" from Les Misérables    Dolokhov"Stars" from 
 Les Misérables    Balaga"Sit Down\, You're Rockin' the Boat" from Guys a
 nd Dolls    Mary Bolkonskaya"I Dreamed a Dream" from Les Misérables    O
 ld Prince Bolkonsky"Edelweiss" from The Sound of Music
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<h2>  Come audition for the Fall MainStage M
 usical:<br />  Natasha\, Pierre &amp\; the Great Comet of 1812</h2><p><st
 rong>Music Auditions: 10-2:30pm in Seitz Lounge in Evans Music Center</st
 rong><br /><strong>Dance Auditions: 3-5pm in Fir Acres Blackbox</strong><
 /p><p><em>The Theatre &amp\; Dance and Music Departments will hold pre-au
 ditions this spring for a few roles in the Fall 2026 MainStage Musical.&#
 160\; (Auditions will be held again in Fall 2026 for roles that are not f
 illed.) Sign up on the Call Board in Fir Acres Theatre.</em></p><h4><stro
 ng>Dance Auditions:</strong></h4><p>  For the dance audition performers s
 hould be prepared to learn and perform a short combination demonstrating 
 basic movement ability\, musicality\, coordination\, and performance pres
 ence. Dancers may briefly share any prior training\, technical skills\, o
 r movement strengths they have\, including turns\, leaps\, acro\, or othe
 r dance styles. Audition focus is not only on technical ability\, but als
 o on adaptability\, confidence\, and responsiveness to instruction.</p><h
 4><strong>The music audition will consist of three elements:</strong></h4
 ><ol><li>A range check (warmup)  </li><li>An unaccompanied folk song or p
 op song of your choosing  </li><li>A song from the list below that corres
 ponds to the character you are interested in  </li></ol><div>  The follow
 ing song suggestions for each character draw from a wide range of musical
 s and pop/rock music\, chosen to align with the characters' complexities\
 , emotions\, and the vocal demands of the roles. The list below is certai
 nly not meant to be the only songs we want to hear\, but ideas about the 
 type of song.</div><div><br /><strong>You are expected to bring sheet mus
 ic for your song from this list. If you need help finding the sheet music
  please contact Prof. Cox (<a href="mailto:lc21-1459@lclark.edu" target="
 _blank" rel="noopener">lc21-1459@lclark.edu</a>) or Sue McBerry (<a href=
 "mailto:mcberry@lclark.edu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">mcberry@lclark
 .edu</a>) or email <a href="mailto:theatre@lclark.edu">theatre@lclark.edu
 </a>&#160\;</strong></div><div></div><div>  Pierre Bezukhov</div><ul><li>
 "Anthem" from Chess  </li></ul><div></div><div>  Natasha Rostova</div><ul
 ><li>"I Feel Pretty" from West Side Story  </li></ul><div></div><div>  An
 drey Bolkonsky</div><ul><li>"Johanna (Reprise)" from Sweeney Todd  </li><
 /ul><div></div><div>  Anatole Kuragin</div><ul><li>"Left Behind" from Spr
 ing Awakening  </li></ul><div></div><div>  Hélène Bezukhova</div><ul><l
 i>"The Ladies Who Lunch" from Company  </li></ul><div></div><div>  Marya 
 D</div><ul><li>"Send in the Clowns" from A Little Night Music  </li></ul>
 <div></div><div>  Sonya</div><ul><li>"On My Own" from Les Misérables  </
 li></ul><div></div><div>  Dolokhov</div><ul><li>"Stars" from Les Misérab
 les  </li></ul><div></div><div>  Balaga</div><ul><li>"Sit Down\, You're R
 ockin' the Boat" from Guys and Dolls  </li></ul><div></div><div>  Mary Bo
 lkonskaya</div><ul><li>"I Dreamed a Dream" from Les Misérables  </li></u
 l><div></div><div>  Old Prince Bolkonsky</div><ul><li>"Edelweiss" from Th
 e Sound of Music  </li></ul>
