SUMMARY:Senior Recital: Mia Raju\, viola
DESCRIPTION:This concert traces a journey through contrasting musical voi
 ces and eras\, featuring works by Bach\, York Bowen\, Bohuslav Martinů\,
  and Dmitri Shostakovich. Through these works\, this recital explores the
 mes of introspection\, resilience\, and expressive storytelling across mu
 sical traditions. Spanning from the intimate clarity of the Baroque to th
 e expressive intensity of the 20th century\, the program highlights the v
 iola's unique ability to bridge lyricism and depth. This performance will
  be live streamed here. (https://vimeo.com/event/4079258)Parking at Lewis
  &amp\; Clark - For events in Evans Auditorium\, Agnes Flanagan Chapel\, 
 or Diane Gregg Pavilion\, enter at Gate 2 and park in Upper Griswold\, Lo
 wer Griswold\, or Fir Acres Lots (see: campus map (https://www.lclark.edu
 /live/files/7676-campus-map)).Parking permits are required during the aca
 demic year between Monday through Friday\, 7am to 7pm. Please see the Vis
 iting Campus page (https://www.lclark.edu/visit/parking_and_transportatio
 n/visitor_parking/) for additional details. For weekday events before 7pm
 \, visitors may purchase day passes online (https://lclark.t2hosted.com/A
 ccount/Portal) or via QR codes posted in all major parking lots.
