SUMMARY:Collective Crisis Peer Support Group: The Good Grief Network
DESCRIPTION:We are all carrying a great deal right now: grief\, anger\, p
 ressure\, urgency\, and fatigue from our world's inter-connected crises. 
 These are intense and heavy times. This group is designed as a space to u
 nburden some of that weight\, feel less alone in it\, and build emotional
  resilience alongside others engaged with these issues.What this is:Suppo
 rtive\, small-group meetings following Good Grief Network's10-Step Progra
 m. Together we'll process emotions\, share openly\, and explore practices
  that help transform overwhelm into meaning\, steadiness\, and connection
 . This space is a balm for burnout\; something us humans desperately need
 .Who it's for:Anyone — students\, professionals\, and community members
  at L&amp\;C and beyond — who feels exhausted\, disconnected\, or demor
 alized by the state of our world\, and who would benefit from a space to 
 reflect and reconnect to purpose in community.What sessions include:Group
  sharing\, grounding practices\, journaling\, poetry\, and thoughtful res
 ources. The space will be co-facilitated by Katia Kupelina and Frances St
 ar\; both certified facilitators with Good Grief Network.DetailsWhere: Le
 wis &amp\; Clark Graduate Campus — Corbett House\, Room 109When: Wednes
 days\, 6–8 PM (April 15 – June 24\, 2026)(No session May 6)Group size
 : Limited to 13 participantsCost: $25 per session or $200 (discount code 
 available) for the full 10-session series.Scholarships are available. We 
 will not turn you away for lack of funds. Participants can emailhello@goo
 dgriefnetwork.org (mailto:hello@goodgriefnetwork.org)before registering t
 o ask about scholarship options.CLICK HERE TO REGISTER A SPOT! (https://b
 it.ly/4tUNrZ1)
