X-LIVEWHALE-COST:<p>This event offers scholarships to address the cost of
  attendance\, should you need it. Standard pricing starts at $25/session 
 or $200 for all 10 sessions.&#160\;</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-CONTACT-INFO:<p>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:hello@good
 griefnetwork.org">hello@goodgriefnetwork.org</a> or <a href="mailto:leads
 erve@lclark.edu">leadserve@lclark.edu</a>&#160\;</p>
X-LIVEWHALE-SUMMARY:<div>\n  An in-person <strong>collective crisis peer 
 support group</strong> through the Good Grief Network will be held at the
  Lewis &amp\; Clark Graduate Campus in Corbett House this spring (April 1
 5–June 24\, Wednesdays 6–8 PM). This space is intended for students\,
  professionals\, and community members who are feeling the emotional weig
 ht of our times—grief\, anger\, burnout\, fatigue\, and the strain of l
 iving through interconnected global crises—and who may benefit from a s
 upportive space to process in community.\n</div>\n<div>\n  <p>\n    Follo
 wing Good Grief Network's 10-Step Program\, the group offers a facilitate
 d container for reflection\, grounding practices\, and group sharing. Tog
 ether\, participants will explore ways to metabolize overwhelm\, reconnec
 t with meaning and purpose\, and build emotional resilience. Individuals 
 may attend drop-in sessions or participate in the full series. Facilitate
 d by Katia Kupelian and Frances Star.\n  </p>\n</div>
X-LIVEWHALE-TAGS:collaboration|community engagement|faculty|interdiscipli
 nary|open to the public|staff|student|sustainability|TCK
