 and Other Pleasures of the Writer's Craft</span></em></strong> and <em><s
 trong><span class="wixui-rich-text__text">100 Tricks Every Boy Can Do: Ho
 w My Brother Disappeared</span></strong></em>. His most recent book is th
 e poetry collection <strong><em><span class="wixui-rich-text__text">As th
 e Sky Begins to Change</span></em></strong> (Red Hen Press\, 2024). He ha
 s taught writing in dozens of schools and community centers\, and in Scot
 land\, Italy\, Mexico\, and Bhutan. In 2018 he was named Oregon's 9th Poe
 t Laureate for a two-year term. The <a href="https://archiveswest.orbisca
 scade.org/ark:80444/xv728701">Kim Stafford's archive</a> is also held at 
 Lewis &amp\; Clark.</p><p><strong><a href="https://carolyn-supinka.square
 space.com/">Carolyn Supinka</a></strong> (she/her) is an interdisciplinar
