DESCRIPTION:This ten-movement work for choirs\, soloists\, and orchestra 
 offers a powerful and personal meditation on grief and hope. Featured art
 ists: Madeleine Tran\, soprano\; Lisa Neher\, mezzo-soprano\; Brandon Mic
 hael\, tenor\; and Nicolas Vilches '26\, baritone\, with Katherine FitzGi
 bbon\, conductor.  Lewis &amp\; Clark's featured ensembles include Cappel
 la Nova and Community Chorale (Katherine FitzGibbon\, director)\, Voces A
 uream (John Cox\, director)\, and the Lewis &amp\; Clark Orchestra (Lance
  Inouye\, director).Tickets are on sale now! (https://app.arts-people.com
 /index.php?ticketing=lccmd) This performance will be live streamed here. 
 (https://vimeo.com/event/4079258)  &#160\;Parking at Lewis &amp\; Clark -
  For events in Evans Auditorium\, Agnes Flanagan Chapel\, or Diane Gregg 
 Pavilion\, enter at Gate 2 and park in Upper Griswold\, Lower Griswold\, 
 or Fir Acres Lots (see: campus map (https://www.lclark.edu/live/files/767
 6-campus-map)).Parking permits are required during the academic year betw
 een Monday through Friday\, 7am to 7pm. Please see the Visiting Campus pa
 ge (https://www.lclark.edu/visit/parking_and_transportation/visitor_parki
 ng/) for additional details. For weekday events before 7pm\, visitors may
  purchase day passes online (https://lclark.t2hosted.com/Account/Portal) 
 or via QR codes posted in all major parking lots.
