 showing up as irritability\, mood shifts\, anxiety\, depression\, grief\,
  self-doubt\, brain fog\, and heightened emotional insecurity. These expe
 riences can disrupt relationships\, work functioning\, and a client's sen
 se of identity and self-efficacy. Many clients report little preparation\
 , limited validation\, and inconsistent guidance on what to expect or how
  to cope.</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  This skills-based training e
 quips clinicians and helping professionals with practical\, trauma-inform
 ed\, and culturally responsive tools to support clients who are navigatin
 g menopause-related mental health and life-transition stress.</p><p style
 ="line-height: 1.5\;">  Presenter Audrianna J. Gurr\, LPC\, CADCI\, menta
