DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260820T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260820T130000
LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Challenges and Complexities in Clinical Supervision (Online)
DESCRIPTION:This workshop is designed for clinical supervisors to explore
  challenges and complexities in their supervision practice.We will discus
 s some common challenges that arise for professional counselors\, and how
  these complex\, multi-layered difficulties can result in a variety of no
 t-so-helpful supervisee responses\, sometimes leading to Licensing Board 
 investigations and possible disciplinary actions. With a strong superviso
 ry alliance\, supervisors can anticipate and proactively address such sit
 uations\, being alert to providing timely assistance in events that affec
 t our supervisees.Participants can expect to engage in active dialogue an
 d exploration of our clinical supervision practices using some examples f
 rom Oregon Licensing Board-identified situations. We will discuss the rol
 e of supervisee non-disclosure and some assumptions supervisors make in c
 linical supervision\, missing opportunities to help supervisees avoid pro
 blematic situations and adverse outcomes in their clinical practice.Durin
 g this training\, participants will:      Discuss strategies that help cl
 inical supervisees recognize their need for guidance          Explore com
 mon pitfalls of supervisee non-disclosure          Discuss supervisor - s
 upervisee relationship strengthening strategies          Examine problema
 tic practice examples from the Oregon Board's 2025 Disciplinary Report   
        Review ACA ethical principles and the Oregon Board's sanctioning c
 onsiderations in these examples          Develop proactive supervisory in
 terventions to address areas of concern          Explore the role of Disc
 iplinary Supervision and other remedial considerations    Details &amp\; 
 RegistrationDate &amp\; Time: Thursday\, August 20\, 2026\, 9 a.m.-12 p.m
 . PT\, OnlineInstructor: James Gurule\, MA\, LPCCost &amp\; Credits: $105
 \, includes 4 CEUs. GSEC Alumni\, Adjuncts\, and Clinical Mental Health S
 upervisors save 20%.Register Online (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/wf1W4MQ?
 epid=a1aUY000002WYQP)Accessibility: We are committed to making our events
  accessible to all needs and abilities. When registering\, please let us 
 know your access needs. Contact us at 503-768-6040 or cce@lclark.edu (mai
 lto:cce@lclark.edu)&#160\;with questions.Please note: Discounted &#x2018\
 ;Student Rate&#x2019\; registrations are for current students only and do
  not include continuing education credit (CEU/PDUs)About the InstructorJa
 mes Gurule\, MA\, LPC (https://parallelpatterns.com/#)\,&#160\;is a licen
 sed professional counselor with over four decades of clinical experience 
 working in community mental health. Practicing as a child and family ther
 apist\, James also provided clinical supervision with agency staff and wa
 s designated as Lead Risk Manager at Lifeworks NW.  James regularly provi
 des professional trainings in ethics\, Solution Focused clinical supervis
 ion and other strength-based supervisory and clinical practices. James ha
 s taught many courses for Lewis &amp\; Clark Graduate School's Center for
  Community Engagement\,&#160\; and Lifeworks NW.New workshops and trainin
 gs are added to our calendar regularly. For the latest on professional de
 velopment related to your specific interests\, sign up for our mailing li
 st! (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735441)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><span style="b
 ackground-color: transparent\;">This workshop is designed for clinical su
 pervisors to explore challenges and complexities in their supervision pra
 ctice.</span></p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><span style="background-co
 lor: transparent\;">We will discuss some common challenges that arise for
  professional counselors\, and how these complex\, multi-layered difficul
 ties can result in a variety of not-so-helpful supervisee responses\, som
 etimes leading to Licensing Board investigations and possible disciplinar
 y actions. With a strong supervisory alliance\, supervisors can anticipat
 e and proactively address such situations\, being alert to providing time
 ly assistance in events that affect our supervisees.</span></p><p style="
 line-height: 1.5\;"><span style="background-color: transparent\;">Partici
 pants can expect to engage in active dialogue and exploration of our clin
 ical supervision practices using some examples from Oregon Licensing Boar
 d-identified situations. We will discuss the role of supervisee non-discl
 osure and some assumptions supervisors make in clinical supervision\, mis
 sing opportunities to help supervisees avoid problematic situations and a
 dverse outcomes in their clinical practice.</span></p><p><strong>During t
 his training\, participants will:</strong></p><ul><li><p style="line-heig
 ht: 1.5\;">      Discuss strategies that help clinical supervisees recogn
 ize their need for guidance    </p></li><li><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"
 >      Explore common pitfalls of supervisee non-disclosure    </p></li><
 li><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">      Discuss supervisor - supervisee re
 lationship strengthening strategies    </p></li><li><p style="line-height
 : 1.5\;">      Examine problematic practice examples from the Oregon Boar
 d's 2025 Disciplinary Report    </p></li><li><p style="line-height: 1.5\;
 ">      Review ACA ethical principles and the Oregon Board's sanctioning 
 considerations in these examples    </p></li><li><p style="line-height: 1
 .5\;">      Develop proactive supervisory interventions to address areas 
 of concern    </p></li><li><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">      Explore th
 e role of Disciplinary Supervision and other remedial considerations    <
 /p></li></ul><hr /><h2><strong>Details &amp\; Registration</strong></h2><
 p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Date &amp\; Time:</strong> Thursday\
 , August 20\, 2026\, 9 a.m.-12 p.m. PT\, Online</p><p style="line-height:
  1.5\;"><strong>Instructor:</strong> James Gurule\, MA\, LPC</p><p style=
 "line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Cost &amp\; Credits:</strong> $105\, include
 s 4 CEUs. GSEC Alumni\, Adjuncts\, and Clinical Mental Health Supervisors
  save 20%.</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong><a class="btn-small-s
 tyle-1" href="https://lclark.tfaforms.net/wf1W4MQ?epid=a1aUY000002WYQP" t
 arget="_blank" rel="noopener">Register Online</a></strong></p><div id="lw
 _widget_30f0017c" class="lw_widget lw_widget_type_blurbs lw_widget_blurbs
  lw_widget_id_7119 lw_widget_accessibility_statement lw_widget_pagination
 "><ul class="lw_widget_results lw_widget_results_blurbs"><li class="lw_it
 em_1"><div class="lw_blurbs_body"><p class="p1" style="font-size: 15px\; 
 line-height: 1.5\;"><em><strong>Accessibility:</strong> We are committed 
 to making our events accessible to all needs and abilities. When register
 ing\, please let us know your access needs. Contact us at 503-768-6040 or
  <a href="mailto:cce@lclark.edu">cce@lclark.edu</a>&#160\;with questions.
 <br/></em></p><p class="p1" style="font-size: 15px\; line-height: 1.5\;">
 <em><strong>Please note:</strong> Discounted &#x2018\;Student Rate&#x2019
 \; registrations are for current students only and <strong>do not</strong
 > include continuing education credit (CEU/PDUs)</em></p></div></li></ul>
 </div><hr /><h2><strong>About the Instructor</strong></h2><p style="line-
 height: 1.5\;"><strong><a href="https://parallelpatterns.com/#">James Gur
 ule\, MA\, LPC</a></strong>\,&#160\;is a licensed professional counselor 
 with over four decades of clinical experience working in community mental
  health. Practicing as a child and family therapist\, James also provided
  clinical supervision with agency staff and was designated as Lead Risk M
 anager at Lifeworks NW.</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  James regularl
 y provides professional trainings in ethics\, Solution Focused clinical s
 upervision and other strength-based supervisory and clinical practices. J
 ames has taught many courses for Lewis &amp\; Clark Graduate School's Cen
 ter for Community Engagement\,&#160\; and Lifeworks NW.</p><div id="lw_wi
 dget_470b39ba" class="lw_widget lw_widget_type_blurbs lw_widget_blurbs lw
 _widget_id_3994 lw_widget_opt_in lw_widget_pagination"><ul class="lw_widg
 et_results lw_widget_results_blurbs"><li class="lw_item_1"><div class="lw
 _blurbs_body"><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><em><strong>New workshops and
  trainings are added to our calendar regularly.</strong> For the latest o
 n professional development related to your specific interests\, <a href="
 https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735441">sign up for our mailing list!</a></e
 m></p></div></li></ul></div>
